From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] texture_cache: give the pressure margin back on real headroom

pressure_margin is what "Out of device memory: keeping N MiB more free" raises, 512 MiB at a
time, under the budget. Recovery is one 128 MiB step per 600 frames with no new pressure event.
Pressure that arrives in bursts resets that counter every time, so the margin never comes back.
A 445-second run walked it 2560/3328 -> 2048/2816 -> 1536/2304 -> 1024/1792 -> 1024/1280 ->
1024/1024 and stayed at the floor for the last 253 reports.

At the floor the collector runs every frame (total_used_memory > minimum_memory) and in
aggressive mode evicts anything not touched for ten frames, so intermittently used images are
deleted and re-created every frame: created 6616, deleted 6490, downloaded 2043 images in 600
frames. That churn is the flicker.

Recover from the driver's own free figure instead: half the margin back once it reports the
margin plus a gigabyte free, and only after 120 frames of that headroom. A run that still needs
the room keeps it - any new pressure event resets the counter and raises the margin again.

What this can break: if the driver reports free memory that a fragmented heap cannot actually
hand out, the collector gives room back too early, allocations fail again, and images go
unbacked (black or flickering textures) or the session dies. The extra gigabyte over the
margin, and the 120-frame stretch, make that unlikely; they are not a guarantee. The step is
512 MiB, the same size the pressure path takes, so a wrong guess is undone by the next event.

Checked: applies to the tree the 0410-0413 stack produces. Not run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -616,9 +616,24 @@
                         budget_check_frames = 0; // thresholds are recomputed below
                         LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "Out of device memory: keeping {} MiB more free",
                                     pressure_margin >> 20);
-                    } else if (pressure_margin != 0 && ++pressure_quiet_frames % 600 == 0) {
-                        pressure_margin -= (std::min)(pressure_margin, 128_MiB);
-                        budget_check_frames = 0;
+                    } else if (pressure_margin != 0) {
+                        // Give the room back on the driver's own free figure, not on an event-free
+                        // interval: bursty pressure reset that counter every time, so the margin
+                        // never came back and the collector evicted live images every frame.
+                        if constexpr (requires { runtime.GetDeviceMemoryUsage(); }) {
+                            const u64 budget = runtime.GetDeviceMemoryBudget();
+                            const u64 usage = runtime.GetDeviceMemoryUsage();
+                            const u64 free = budget > usage ? budget - usage : 0;
+                            if (free >= pressure_margin + 1_GiB) {
+                                if (++pressure_quiet_frames >= 120) {
+                                    pressure_margin -= (std::min)(pressure_margin, 512_MiB);
+                                    pressure_quiet_frames = 0;
+                                    budget_check_frames = 0;
+                                }
+                            } else {
+                                pressure_quiet_frames = 0;
+                            }
+                        }
                     }
                 }
             }
